<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan lowers fuel oil bunker prices by $4/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan lowers fuel oil bunker prices by $4/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has lowered its bunker fuel prices by $4 per tonne effective March 4, a company statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Posted prices for 180, 280 and 380 centistoke bunker fuel delivered at the ports of Keelung, Hualien, Taichung and Suao were decreased by $4 per tonne, to $119. Term prices were also cut $4 to $116 per tonne.</p>
<p>Spot and term bunker C grade were also lowered by $4 to $117 and $114 respectively.</p>
<p>CPC is Taiwan's monopoly supplier of bunker fuels.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703082)</p>
</text>
